In the fixed1900 state window, teacher E85 has1900speed>.5 samples and trackingRMS.002032111rad; E121 has1320 and.001877705rad. E121 tracking is globally close to requested motion, yet its supported tarsus5 forward-motion fraction is.229965157 versus teacher.129071379. In E121 backward323states this fraction is.470527404 and interval-native slip2.868272302mm/s, compared with forward.125532448/1.629617204. These are descriptive associations; tip velocity is not direct propulsive force. Native[.5,10) overall slip is1.973669833 versus teacher1.415031299, kept distinct from endpoint-group interval(.495,9.995]. Teacher tendon commands differ, but E121 legtendonp50.199902892–.199987240 is near teacher.2. This supports prioritizing within-leg native recruitment waveform over global servo/tendon gain; it does not prove a biological mechanism.

Final source review: parent-e122-final-source-review.json. Original analysis: e122-support-transfer/summary.json andcomparison.png. Independent saved-data review: e122-support-transfer/parent-final-review.json (accepted diagnostic only). Original E121 F3passes/F4F5fails, cycles0 and all final F1–F8 requirements remain unchanged. No candidate adopted.

